<div class="page">
<header class="masthead">
<p class="eyebrow">Fortress revival &middot; foundations rewrite &middot; 2026-10-26</p>
<h1>Thirteen new reasons, for your yes</h1>
<p class="standfirst">On 26 October, at 07:42 and 07:48 UTC, you approved rewriting the reasons under some of your decisions, through a test built to mislead, before anything enters the record. The rewrite and the test are done. References sit at the end of each section.</p>
</header>

<nav class="parts" aria-label="Sections">
<h2>Five sections</h2>
<ol>
<li><a href="#asks">What this page asks</a></li>
<li><a href="#test">The test, in plain words</a></li>
<li><a href="#answers">The answers these texts assume</a></li>
<li><a href="#entries">The thirteen entries</a>
<ol>
<li><a href="#e1">4.1 The team's later word wins</a></li>
<li><a href="#e2">4.2 One library for both paths</a></li>
<li><a href="#e3">4.3 The exclusion rule and the flat numbers</a></li>
<li><a href="#e4">4.4 The default bound is Any</a></li>
<li><a href="#e5">4.5 The phases of the work</a></li>
<li><a href="#e6">4.6 The goal and its measure</a></li>
<li><a href="#e7">4.7 Walk runs the checker after the switch-over</a></li>
<li><a href="#e8">4.8 Walk's choice of coercion until then</a></li>
<li><a href="#e9">4.9 Unboxed doubles are required</a></li>
<li><a href="#e10">4.10 Arrays of doubles stored as double[]</a></li>
<li><a href="#e11">4.11 The open array questions, and your lean</a></li>
<li><a href="#e12">4.12 The natives' form</a></li>
<li><a href="#e13">4.13 Abstract members are declared in the component</a></li>
</ol></li>
<li><a href="#after">What happens after your yes</a></li>
</ol>
</nav>

<section id="asks" class="part">
<h2><span class="num">1</span>What this page asks</h2>
<p>Thirteen of your entries in the record of decisions have new reasons, written after the foundations review. Nothing enters the record until you say yes. You can answer "yes", or name an entry to change by its section number, such as 4.4.</p>
<div class="sources"><span class="label">References</span>
<ul>
<li>The thirteen entries and your approval: <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/60aaeb6bb0f74dcb6018b0b5ceb268b0834da50e/explorations/reviews/foundations/rewrite-results.md#what-was-rewritten">the rewrite's results, "What was rewritten"</a>.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>

<section id="test" class="part">
<h2><span class="num">2</span>The test, in plain words</h2>
<p>The test checks that the new texts lead the coordinator to the right choice. The coordinator is the session that plans the work and runs the agents.</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Four cases.</strong> Each is a case that a planner or a worker could bring to the coordinator. A planner is the agent that drafts a batch of work; a worker builds one piece of it. The cases were written before the new texts existed, so that the old texts lead the wrong way.</li>
<li><strong>Three readers.</strong> Two agents each acted as the coordinator, on a copy of the repository without the review. One had the old texts, the other the new ones. A third agent graded both answers without knowing which reader had which texts. Each case scores 3 points: 2 for the decision, 1 for the sources cited.</li>
<li><strong>The result.</strong> The new texts: 12 of 12. The old texts: 10 of 12. Both readers cited their sources in full. The old texts lost one point of decision in each of two cases.</li>
<li><strong>Where the old texts misled: the order traits' self type.</strong> The order traits are the library's traits for comparing values. Their self type stands for the type that implements the trait. A planner proposed to copy the compiler's prelude's spelling of it, <code>comprises T</code>, into the one library, as "the team's later word". The compiler's prelude is the compiler's own small library. The one library is the library of walk, the interpreter; both paths are to use it. The reader with the old texts dropped the copy, which was right, but on a weaker ground: the library's own practice. And it kept the copy open, to be tested by a probe and then put to you as a question. A probe is a small experiment. The reader had the dates: Naden's text of 31 August 2012 is later than Steele's prelude edits of 5 and 6 June 2012. But no old text made the date decide. The new later-word and one-library entries do.</li>
<li><strong>Where the old texts misled: <code>System</code> on the compiled path.</strong> <code>System</code> is the component, the part of the library, that gives a program its arguments and its environment. A planner proposed to keep the compiler's own <code>System</code>, <code>CompilerSystem</code>, on the compiled path after the switch-over. The switch-over is the point where the compiled path moves onto the one library and the compiler's prelude is deleted. The reader with the old texts refused, but offered a <code>CompilerSystem</code> bridge as one option of a question to you. The old one-library entry gives no reason for one library. The new one gives yours: the switch-over exists so that walk's library is not ported into the compiler's.</li>
<li><strong>The other two cases.</strong> A worker offered to make a defect of the code generator a rule of the language. Another offered to fix a checker defect by copying a range trait from the compiler's prelude into the one library. In both cases, both readers chose right.</li>
</ol>
<div class="sources"><span class="label">References</span>
<ul>
<li>Point 1: <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/60aaeb6bb0f74dcb6018b0b5ceb268b0834da50e/explorations/reviews/foundations/evidence/trap-test/questions.md">the four cases</a>, and <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/60aaeb6bb0f74dcb6018b0b5ceb268b0834da50e/explorations/reviews/foundations/evidence/trap-test/key.md">their key</a>, written before the new texts; <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/60aaeb6bb0f74dcb6018b0b5ceb268b0834da50e/explorations/reviews/foundations/rewrite-results.md#the-trap-test">the rewrite's results, "The trap test"</a>.</li>
<li>Point 2: the same, "Its form": two worktrees at <code>bedc80b01</code>, without the review's folder and its conversation note.</li>
<li>Point 3: <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/60aaeb6bb0f74dcb6018b0b5ceb268b0834da50e/explorations/reviews/foundations/evidence/trap-test/grades.md#3-totals">the grades, section 3, "Totals"</a>.</li>
<li>Point 4: <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/60aaeb6bb0f74dcb6018b0b5ceb268b0834da50e/explorations/reviews/foundations/evidence/trap-test/grades.md#2-where-one-answer-scored-lower">the grades, section 2</a>, scenario 2; <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/60aaeb6bb0f74dcb6018b0b5ceb268b0834da50e/explorations/reviews/foundations/evidence/trap-test/grades.md#4-the-positions-entries-that-the-scenarios-quote">section 4</a>, POSITIONS 26 and 37; <code>self-typed-bodies-judgement.md</code> lines 22 to 24.</li>
<li>Point 5: the grades, section 2, scenario 4; section 4, POSITIONS 37; <code>POSITIONS-history.md</code> line 466.</li>
<li>Point 6: <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/60aaeb6bb0f74dcb6018b0b5ceb268b0834da50e/explorations/reviews/foundations/evidence/trap-test/grades.md#1-scores-by-scenario">the grades, section 1</a>, scenarios 1 and 3.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>

<section id="answers" class="part">
<h2><span class="num">3</span>The answers these texts assume</h2>
<p>Four of your answers are still open. The texts are written under the default of each. If you answer another way, the texts change as each point says.</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Phase 3 closes with climb batch 22c, over fourteen components.</strong> Phase 3 is the work that makes the type checker accept the library's core components without error. A component is one part of the library, such as <code>List</code>. A climb batch is one run of the workflow in which agents build a set of rungs; a rung is one piece of work. The distance stage is the tool that counts the checker's errors over the library's twelve core components. The fourteen are those twelve, plus the two that <code>List</code> imports. Default: yes. If no: the one-library and phases entries count the twelve, not the fourteen, and the phases entry counts 40 other components, not 38.</li>
<li><strong>The 38 other components block a later step, not the switch-over.</strong> The later step is the one at which walk, the interpreter, runs the checker on its programs, after the switch-over. Each component is cleared before that step, or before the first program that needs it. The judgement wrote 40, but two of the 40 are <code>List</code>'s imports, which phase 3 now counts. Default: yes. If no: the one-library and phases entries say that the switch-over also needs those components to pass the checker and the code generator, and the entry on walk and the checker says they are cleared by then.</li>
<li><strong>Three one-word answers.</strong> Defaults: drop "functions" from what the bound's entry says <code>Any</code> holds; strike the sentence "The implementers' later word also outweighs unfinished text." from the later-word entry; move the flat-numbers entry's two "Why" sentences to the record's history, the file that keeps each entry's earlier texts. If you keep any of these, that entry keeps its old words: the bound's entry says "tuples, functions and <code>()</code>"; the later-word entry keeps the sentence; the flat-numbers entry keeps its two sentences and drops the one that calls the prelude's flat numbers "not a ground".</li>
<li><strong>Your lean toward the class loader, recorded as a lean to confirm.</strong> On 20 September you leaned toward the class loader as the way to give an <code>RR64</code> array, made through the library's generic array traits, a Java <code>double[]</code> store. The class loader is the part of the compiled path that makes Java classes while a program runs. Default: record it. If no: the array-questions entry drops its new sentence, and the array-store entry drops its last clause, which points to the lean.</li>
</ol>
<div class="sources"><span class="label">References</span>
<ul>
<li>Point 1: "Depends on an open answer" under <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/60aaeb6bb0f74dcb6018b0b5ceb268b0834da50e/explorations/reviews/foundations/evidence/rewrite/c1/proposals.md#p-37">P-37</a> and <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/60aaeb6bb0f74dcb6018b0b5ceb268b0834da50e/explorations/reviews/foundations/evidence/rewrite/c1/proposals.md#p-42">P-42</a> (chunk one) and <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/60aaeb6bb0f74dcb6018b0b5ceb268b0834da50e/explorations/reviews/foundations/evidence/rewrite/c2/proposals.md#p-33">P-33</a> (chunk two); the twelve, <code>explorations/coordinator/tools/distance/run.sh</code> lines 85 to 87; <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/60aaeb6bb0f74dcb6018b0b5ceb268b0834da50e/explorations/reviews/foundations/judgement.md#5-phase-3s-close-his-framing-is-sound-and-22c-carries-four-rungs">judgement section 5</a>; <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/60aaeb6bb0f74dcb6018b0b5ceb268b0834da50e/explorations/reviews/foundations/judgement.md#9-for-pavol">section 9</a>, decision 1.</li>
<li>Point 2: "Depends on an open answer" under P-37 (chunk one), and P-33 and <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/60aaeb6bb0f74dcb6018b0b5ceb268b0834da50e/explorations/reviews/foundations/evidence/rewrite/c2/proposals.md#p-12">P-12</a> (chunk two); the 40 and their 624 errors, F-290; <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/60aaeb6bb0f74dcb6018b0b5ceb268b0834da50e/explorations/reviews/foundations/judgement.md#tenet-6-the-phase-order-p-33-holds-text">judgement tenet 6</a>; section 9, decision 2.</li>
<li>Point 3: "Depends on an open answer" under P-42, <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/60aaeb6bb0f74dcb6018b0b5ceb268b0834da50e/explorations/reviews/foundations/evidence/rewrite/c1/proposals.md#p-26">P-26</a> and <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/60aaeb6bb0f74dcb6018b0b5ceb268b0834da50e/explorations/reviews/foundations/evidence/rewrite/c1/proposals.md#p-43">P-43</a> (chunk one); section 9, decision 4; review queue items 218, 215, 219 and 220.</li>
<li>Point 4: "Depends on an open answer" under <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/60aaeb6bb0f74dcb6018b0b5ceb268b0834da50e/explorations/reviews/foundations/evidence/rewrite/c2/proposals.md#p-84">P-84</a> and <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/60aaeb6bb0f74dcb6018b0b5ceb268b0834da50e/explorations/reviews/foundations/evidence/rewrite/c2/proposals.md#p-85">P-85</a> (chunk two); <a href="https://github.com/palimondo/fortress/blob/60aaeb6bb0f74dcb6018b0b5ceb268b0834da50e/explorations/reviews/foundations/judgement.md#tenet-7-unboxed-doubles-and-double-arrays-p-17-p-84-holds-text">judgement tenet 7</a>; section 9, decision 6.</li>
