<li>New, from the judgement, for your yes: the order's ground is in the team's build. The compiled path runs the checker first, then code generation and the run time. The natives, the library functions whose body is Java, define the switch-over.</li>
<li>Phase 3's exit changes, from "no error on the interpreter's whole library" to no error and no crash over the fourteen components. It counts only under the compile command's own setting, with the bound <code>Any</code>, and with the export check reading operators and abstract members. The export check is the checker's test that each component provides what its api, its interface, lists. You agreed that "whole" was wrong. The new exit restates one that you approved, so it is yours to confirm: it is your open answer on phase 3.</li>
