<h3>The new text</h3>
<div class="entry-text"><p>P-33 <strong>The work toward microGPT compiled follows the phases, in the order that the curator approved.</strong> These phases are steps of the work, not the compiler's phases, and they are numbered 3 to 6, after two earlier ones. The order's ground is in the team's implementation on the JVM (P-26 defines the layers): the compiled path runs the checker first, and code generation and the run time after it, and the natives define the switch-over. Phase 3: the compiled checker reports no error and no crash over the fourteen components, which are the distance stage's twelve and the two that <code>List</code> imports, <code>CovariantCollection</code> and <code>OneShotFlag</code> (F-53 defines the distance and holds its value). The zero counts only when the distance stage runs under the setting of <code>fortress compile</code> itself (F-289), once that command sets the bound <code>Any</code> (P-42), and with the export check comparing the top-level symbolic operators, which it skips today (row 782, P-155), and requiring each <code>abstract</code> member of an api in its component (P-158). Phase 4, the switch-over: first the natives, the library's <code>builtinPrimitive</code> bindings made to run on the compiled path; then the compiled path reads the interpreter's library, and the compiler's prelude is deleted. The switch-over needs two zeros over the fourteen (P-37): the checker's, which phase 3 brings, and the code generator's, which phase 4 brings. The code generator's half was unmeasured when the curator approved the order; it now refuses 52 declarations of the twelve that the checker passes (F-34). The library's 38 other components, outside the fourteen, do not block the switch-over (F-290 counts the errors of the 40 outside the twelve, <code>List</code>'s two imports among them): each is cleared before the step at which walk runs the checker (P-12), or before the first program that needs it. Phase 5, microGPT compiles: its static types, 